      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MARY H. WILLIAMS, ESQ., Solicitor General, Salem, Oregon; on behalf of the Petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "KANNON K. SHANMUGAM, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "RICHARD L. WOLF, ESQ., Portland, Oregon; appointed by this Court; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. WILLIAMS: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The eight amendment requires that a sentencing jury in a capital case must consider mitigation, which this Court consistently has defined as related to a defendant's background, character, or the circumstances of the offense. The Oregon Supreme Court in this case has broadly construed circumstances of the offense to include evidence that is inconsistent with the defendant's guilt. That holding is not constitutionally compelled and does not further the purpose of having the sentencing jury consider mitigation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. WILLIAMS: That's correct, Mr. Chief Justice. The Oregon Supreme Court's conclusion is very broad, that any alibi evidence comes in, and, as the dissent notes, that it also would not be limited simply to alibi evidence, but any evidence that is inconsistent with the guilt verdict in this case that would form a basis for arguing that doubt about the defendant's guilt should be a factor that the jury considers in responding to the mitigation question that"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SHANMUGAM: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: It does not constitute cruel and unusual punishment to prohibit a capital defendant from"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: That seems to be very strange, because I think our cases require -- require that for death eligibility, and --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0002-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Then there was really no basis for your motion to dismiss the writ as improvidently granted, if that's true."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, I'm not being tricky about it. I want to know if we have to go to the words \"otherwise relevant\" in the Oregon statute -- \"otherwise relevant,\" particularly in respect to this question of residual doubt."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wolf",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Oregon Supreme Court did not say residual doubt was admissible. And residual doubt was never argued to the trial court, to the Oregon Supreme Court; and, therefore, whether or not it can come in --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wolf",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, we would intend to call her."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Why -- because you mentioned, earlier, about the defect in the trial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wolf",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WOLF: The convictions -- well, the defect was in the penalty phase."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wolf",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "-- that the alibi in this case was -- really was offered as impeachment of the codefendants. The codefendants are really the only evidence that links the defendant to these crimes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: General Williams, I have one question. I'm not sure it goes to our eighth amendment question before us, but I honestly don't understand what your statute is all about."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Williams",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. WILLIAMS: Justice Scalia, we copied from Texas on those special issues. And so, in the guilt phase, what you have to establish is the defendant acted intentionally."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Williams",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. WILLIAMS: -- finding, beyond intentional, that the State has to then establish in the penalty phase."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-04-928",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
      "evidence_id": "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, Ms. Williams. The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
